{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I understand you’ve been having abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting again. Can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s the same as last week. Any time I try to eat or drink, I feel sick and start vomiting. The pain is right here in my upper belly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You were just here a week ago for similar symptoms. Since you have a G-tube, are you still able to take your feeds through it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the tube feeds are going okay. I haven’t had any issues with those. But anything by mouth makes me feel worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Given your history of gastric bypass and the GJ ulcer before, this could be gastritis. We’ll start you on IV fluids to rehydrate you and give you some anti-nausea medication."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds good. Do you think it’s another ulcer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We don’t know for sure yet. Your CT scan from earlier didn’t show a blockage, which is reassuring. But we may need an endoscopy soon to look more closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember the last time I had that, they found the ulcer near the connection. Will they do that again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the GI team will likely schedule an outpatient endoscopy next week. For now, we’ll focus on getting your symptoms under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I’ve also been worried because my belly wound has some drainage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I noticed that too. There’s some serous fluid at the base, and the wound is slightly open. We’ll keep it packed and clean. It doesn’t look infected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good, I was worried about that. And my meds—I’m still on lansoprazole and rifaximin, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’re continuing both. We’re also adding sucralfate four times a day. It coats the stomach and helps protect the lining while it heals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from last time. It helps with ulcers, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s especially useful for people with your surgical history. We’ll give it to you through your G-tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s good. And for pain, can I still use the hydrocodone if it gets bad?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You have hydro*mor*phone—Dilaudid—available every three hours as needed. But we’ll try to keep it minimal. The lansoprazole and sucralfate should help reduce irritation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll only use it if I really need to."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re also on ondansetron for nausea, which we’ll give every 12 hours as needed. Let the nurse know if you’re still feeling sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be here long?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you for a couple of days to make sure you’re stable. If your symptoms improve and labs stay normal, you could go home by Thursday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2174-02-17 18:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds manageable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2174-02-18 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2174-02-18 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better, actually. I haven’t vomited since yesterday evening, and the pain is less intense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2174-02-18 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. Your labs from last night were normal—white count, kidney function, everything looks good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2174-02-18 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s probably just inflammation, not an infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2174-02-18 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, no signs of infection. Your symptoms are most consistent with gastritis—stomach lining irritation—likely related to your surgical anatomy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2174-02-18 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the reflux? I used to have that all the time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2174-02-18 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your reflux is listed in your history, and while it’s improved, it can still contribute. That’s why we keep you on high-dose lansoprazole."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2174-02-18 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. And my mental health meds—are they still being given?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2174-02-18 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, fluoxetine and aripiprazole are being given daily through your G-tube. Lorazepam for anxiety is also continued three times a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2174-02-18 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ve been feeling anxious about being back in the hospital."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2174-02-18 09:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely understandable. We’re here to support you. The good news is you’re on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2174-02-19 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’ve reviewed everything, and you’re doing well. The GI team saw you yesterday and will set up your endoscopy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2174-02-19 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2174-02-19 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll discharge you this afternoon. Your symptoms have improved, and you’re back to your baseline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2174-02-19 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the sucralfate? Do I keep taking that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2174-02-19 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, four times a day for now. It helps protect your stomach while we figure out the exact cause with the endoscopy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2174-02-19 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I need to follow up with the weight loss surgery clinic?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2174-02-19 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and GI will contact you to schedule the endoscopy. Keep using your G-tube for meds and feeds, and avoid eating by mouth for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2174-02-19 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2174-02-19 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get the discharge papers ready, and you should be home by early afternoon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2174-02-19 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check-in before discharge. Any new pain or nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2174-02-19 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, still feeling much better. Wound is a little sore, but not bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2174-02-19 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send instructions for wound care home with you. Keep it clean and monitor for redness or pus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2174-02-19 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. And I’ll call if I start vomiting again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2174-02-19 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Also reach out if you have fever, severe pain, or can’t keep your feeds down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2174-02-19 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll stay in touch with the clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2174-02-19 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your discharge orders are in. You’ll get a call from GI soon to schedule the endoscopy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2174-02-19 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2174-02-19 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2174-02-19 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will be in shortly with your discharge paperwork. You’re cleared to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2174-02-19 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great, I’m ready to go."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2174-02-19 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—keep taking all your medications as prescribed, especially the sucralfate before meals and at bedtime."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2174-02-19 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll set reminders. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2174-02-19 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Feel better soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2174-02-19 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—you’re feeling stable and ready for discharge?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2174-02-19 16:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’m ready. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2174-02-19 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re discharged. Take care and follow up as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2174-02-19 16:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Have a good day."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2174-02-17 18:14:00",
    "admission_end": "2174-02-19 16:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for recurrent epigastric pain, nausea, and vomiting shortly after a prior hospitalization for similar symptoms. She has a complex history including Roux-en-Y gastric bypass and gastrostomy tube placement due to a previous GJ anastomotic ulcer. She remained on G-tube feeds throughout and was treated with IV fluids, anti-emetics, and continued proton-pump inhibition with lansoprazole. Sucralfate was added for gastric protection. Her symptoms improved over two days, and labs remained normal. The GI team evaluated her and will arrange an outpatient endoscopy to further investigate the cause of her abdominal pain. She was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to continue medications, avoid oral intake, and follow up with both the weight loss surgery clinic and GI.",
    "problems": [
      "Dehydration",
      "Unspecified gastritis and gastroduodenitis, without mention of hemorrhage",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Gastrostomy status",
      "Bariatric surgery status"
    ]
  }
}
